# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
#
# The Dockerfile uses `COPY . .` — without this file the entire repo (cache,
# docs site, agent worktrees, secrets) is shipped to the build daemon. That
# inflates build time and risks baking sensitive paths into image layers.
#
# Rules of thumb:
#   - Anything regenerated by the build (bin/, coverage, generated docs).
#   - Anything that holds secrets or local state (.env, .claude*, .config/).
#   - Anything purely cosmetic for the repo (README, LICENSE, docs site).
# =============================================================================

# Version control & CI metadata
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Build outputs
bin/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.test
*.out

# Local caches & runtime data
.cache/
.config/
data/
.stromboli-worktrees/

# Editor / devcontainer
.devcontainer/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Secrets & local credentials — must never enter an image layer
.claude/
.claude-secrets/
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Documentation source — published separately, not needed in runtime image
docs/
site/
overrides/
mkdocs.yml
*.md
LICENSE
licenses.tpl
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES

# Tests — production image doesn't need them
tests/

# Other
.DS_Store
